    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d545">

                <pb facs="0772" n="673" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg673"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/3117: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gordon</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-03-12T13:00:00-05:00">March 12, 1936—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 2:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>12. My 8, March 2 [<hi rendition="#italic">6</hi>], 3 p.m.,<anchor n="50"
                        xml:id="d545-f1"/> and 11, March 10, 9 p.m. [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >a.m.</hi>]. President has received another telegram from Mayard to the
                    effect that Quai d’Orsay declines conversations which do not contain precise
                    proposals and will give him until tomorrow to submit them. The Foreign Minister
                    says he does not propose to send any new instructions to Mayard.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gordon</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
